treatment effect on day \eqn{t} described under \code{treatment_effect_decay} in
\code{\link[=sim_markov]{sim_markov()}}. Every term shifts all cutoffs equally, which makes this a
proportional-odds model. The thresholds are\tabular{llllllll}{
   Cutoff \eqn{k} \tab 2 \tab 3 \tab 4 \tab 5 \tab 6 \tab 7 \tab 8 \cr
   \eqn{\alpha_k} \tab -0.6465 \tab -4.9314 \tab -5.2230 \tab -7.4169 \tab -11.5321 \tab -15.2262 \tab -22.0693 \cr
}


and the previous-state effects are\tabular{llllllll}{
   Previous state \eqn{j} \tab 1 \tab 2 \tab 3 \tab 4 \tab 5 \tab 6 \tab 7 \cr
   \eqn{\gamma_j} \tab 0 \tab 0 \tab 6.2218 \tab 7.1412 \tab 9.9809 \tab 14.1645 \tab 19.3517 \cr
