\strong{Treatment effect.} The default \code{treatment_effect} of -0.0730 is the
coefficient fitted to the ACTT-2 data.

\strong{Changing the model.} \code{\link[=sim_markov]{sim_markov()}} expects the thresholds from the
worst state down, so \code{intercepts = rev(alpha)} with \code{alpha} the
\eqn{\alpha_k} above in the order of the table reproduces the preset. Change
an element of \code{alpha} before reversing it to move one threshold.
